PRIVACY POLICY
Last Updated: May 2026

Welcome to our Digital Wallet Application. Your privacy and the security of your financial data are our highest priorities. This Privacy Policy explains how Ramaaz we collects, uses, discloses, and safeguards your information when you use our mobile application.

Please read this privacy policy carefully. If you do not agree with the terms of this privacy policy, please do not access the application.

1. INFORMATION WE COLLECT
As a regulated financial services application, we are required by law to collect certain information to verify your identity and prevent fraud:

Personal Identity Information: Full name, national ID number, passport details, date of birth, and government-issued identification documents (KYC - Know Your Customer).

Contact Information: Email address, phone number, and physical billing address.

Financial Data: Bank account numbers, credit/debit card details, transaction history, wallet balances, and payment metadata.

Device & Technical Data: IP address, device ID, operating system, and biometric data (stored locally on your device for fingerprint/face unlock authorization).

2. HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION
We use the collected data strictly to provide a secure and legally compliant financial service, including to:

Process financial transactions and manage your digital wallet.

Verify your identity in compliance with Central Bank regulations and Anti-Money Laundering (AML) laws.

Detect, prevent, and mitigate fraud, security breaches, or money laundering activities.

Provide customer support and resolve technical or transaction issues.

3. DATA ENCRYPTION & SECURITY
We implement industry-standard financial grade security measures to protect your data. All communication between the app and our servers is strictly encrypted using Transport Layer Security (TLS/SSL). Financial information and sensitive databases are encrypted at rest using advanced encryption standards (AES-256). Biometric tokens never leave your secure device hardware.

4. SHARING AND DISCLOSURE OF DATA
We do not sell or rent your personal or financial data to third parties. We may only share information with:

Regulated partner banks and payment processors necessary to execute your transactions.

Government or law enforcement authorities ONLY when strictly required by applicable financial laws and Central Bank mandates.

5. DATA RETENTION
We retain your personal and financial information only for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this policy and to satisfy statutory regulatory requirements under applicable financial and banking laws.

6. CHANGES TO THIS PRIVACY POLICY
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page and updating the application.

